In posts on Weverse after the show, the boy band&#8217;s members shared messages thanking ARMY for supporting the March 21 performance, and emphasizing how happy they&#8217;re feeling now that it&#8217;s in the books. In one joint statement uploaded to RM&#8217;s profile, the group wrote , &#8220;Hello, this is BTS. After four long years of waiting, the seven members gathered again and faced you in a meaningful space called Gwanghwamun.&#8221;

&#8220;[We] would like to thank everyone for their generous consideration and support so that our return stage can be completed safely,&#8221; it continued, according to the site&#8217;s English translation, shouting out the &#8220;police, firefighters, the government and local governments&#8221; who &#8220;worked hard to make it a safe performance without any major accidents in the midst of large crowds.&#8221;

The Bangtan Boys also expressed &#8220;sincere apologies and thank you to the citizens who endured the inconveniences, such as traffic control and noise, as well as to the merchants and office workers in Gwanghwamun area.&#8221;

&#8220;We will never take for granted the warm consideration for our performance with a broad heart and keep it in our hearts for a long time,&#8221; the statement added. &#8220;And most of all, our dear ARMY who is all and proud of us! Thank you so much for trusting and waiting for us for a long time &#8230; As always, you are our greatest pride.&#8221;

The post comes shortly after the bandmates held their first full-group concert in years at Gwanghwamun Square in Seoul, performing as a unit in honor of their new album, ARIRANG , which dropped Friday (March 20). Some of the members also shared post-show messages to their individual Weverse profiles, such as Jimin, who wrote , &#8220;Yesterday was an unforgettable day thanks to ARMY.&#8221;

&#8220;I was so happy to finally show you the album and performance,&#8221; added the K-pop star. &#8220;There are still a lot of contents, so please look forward to it!!&#8221;

Jin shared a photo of himself on a plane and said, &#8220;ARMY, did you enjoy our comeback show yesterday With the help of many people, we made a comeback safely! I would like to say thank you again to the many people who helped me!&#8221;

J-hope also shared a plane selfie and wrote , &#8220;I&#8217;ll be back safely!!!! Thank you always and I love you!!!&#8221;

Now that the comeback show has wrapped, BTS will travel to the United States to continue with the rollout of ARIRANG . After answering fan questions and performing at a Spotify event in New York City, the septet will appear on The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon .

ARIRANG marks BTS&#8217; first full-length since 2020&#8217;s Be , which topped the Billboard 200 . In the years since, the members have pursued solo projects while also completing their enlistment periods in the South Korean military.
